    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1248">

                <pb facs="1477" n="1279" xml:id="pg1279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Truman Papers</hi></note>
                <head>No. 1248<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to Prime Minister Churchill</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1248-f1"/>]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-25">July 25, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Prime Minister</hi>: …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>We sent you last night a copy of our telegram to Chiang Kai-shek.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1248-f2"/> I am hoping
                    that we will receive a concurrence from him, and that we may be in a position to
                    issue the Proclamation at the earliest possible moment. I shall inform you, as
                    soon as I hear from him, and we will issue the Proclamation jointly from here,
                    if that is satisfactory to you.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry S.
                                Truman</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
